venv
__pycache__
data/cache

# Databases and their backups. `*` does NOT cross a path separator here, so a
# bare `*.bak` matches only the context root and never `data/picks.db.bak-...`.
# That is why the image reached 7.45GB on 2026-08-04: ~30 backups of a 230MB
# database, baked in a layer, while the patterns that were supposed to exclude
# them sat right here looking correct. Every database pattern must name `data/`.
# docker-compose bind-mounts ./backend/data over /app/data at runtime, so the
# live DB is never served from the image regardless.
# Match on the DATABASE NAME, not on a suffix. The suffix list was the bug the
# second time: on 2026-08-11, 0.93GB of backups still reached the context because
# `regrade`/`backfill` scripts name their copies `picks.db.pre-<label>-<stamp>`
# with no `.bak` at all, so `data/*.bak*` missed them and `data/*.db` missed them
# too (the name ends in a digit, not in `.db`). Anything derived from picks.db is
# a database, whatever it is called.
data/picks.db*
data/picks.dev.db*
data/*.db
data/*.db-wal
data/*.db-shm
data/*.bak*
*.db
*.bak
*.bak-*
